-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- memory: the commands the reader uses
-- The reader never touches a memory value (archive/2026-11-11/README.md, "Memory is a signature"): every
-- access is one of the operations of this section and a pointer is abstract outside it. The
-- first group are lib/mem/monad.cub's named operations as they are. The second group are
-- operations the reader needs that the monad does not name yet: each is written here once over
-- lib/mem/memory.cub's function of the same meaning and is listed in archive/2026-11-11/F-cxx.md under
-- "Needs from track M"; when track M's signature of memory commands lands, each becomes that
-- command and nothing outside this section changes.
cx-load : CxU → SK → MPtr → CxEv SV
cx-load u k p = ev-load {lzero} {CxS} {CxR} (cxu-t u) k p
